<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18175" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφεγγ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without light,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῶς ἀ.</span> a light <i>that is no
				light</i> (i. e. to the blind), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1549
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυκτὸς ἀφεγγὲς
			βλέφαρον,</span> of the moon, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				543
			</span></i>; simply, <i>dark,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπῆλυγξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.324
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμίχλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.675
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηϊοτής</span> a <i>night</i>
			battle, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				24.165
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀΐδα . . τὸν ἀφεγγέα χῶρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					372.13
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Cotiaeum</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				8.52
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not visible to the eye,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδμά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					115
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τι . . τυγχάνεις ἀφεγγὲς
			φέρων</span> something <i>ill-starred, unlucky,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1481
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>obscure,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκδοσις</span> Olymp.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.70B.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
